            "content": "Make MySQL the Single Source of Truth The current implementation writes to localStorage first and then synchronizes to MySQL. I want MySQL to become the authoritative data source. Requirements: Do not use localStorage as the primary source for editable content. For every admin save operation: React Form \u2193 POST PHP API \u2193 MySQL UPDATE \u2193 Return updated record \u2193 Update React Query cache (or application state) \u2193 Render UI Only show a success message after MySQL confirms the save. On page load: Load editable content directly from MySQL through the PHP API. Do not rely on localStorage for initial rendering except as an optional offline cache. If the API request fails: Do not update the UI permanently. Display a clear error message. Keep the Save button enabled for retry. Log the error. If offline mode is intentionally supported: Store pending changes in a dedicated offline queue. Automatically synchronize when connectivity returns. Resolve conflicts using a Last Updated timestamp or version number.",
